<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!-- The **video** category, on its own.
	     Apple's CarPlay Developer Guide (2026-10-13), page 15: *"Multiple
	     CarPlay entitlements may not be combined in a single app, unless
	     specifically noted below."* — the only combination it notes is EV
	     charging with fueling (page 15, footnote 1). So a build carries
	     **one** key: this file the video key, `CarTV.audio.entitlements`
	     the audio key.

	     A build that carried both was refused by the system outright: the
	     app never registered as a CarPlay app (*"Set Carplay mode to: 0"*,
	     *"icon launch not enabled"*) and its icon could not be launched.

	     The audio category is the one that fits DrivePlay, and it covers
	     video as well — page 6: *"Audio apps that also provide video
	     playback services in CarPlay must support AirPlay video streaming."*
	     The picture rides that AirPlay route, so this file is the
	     alternative, not the combination. -->
	<key>com.apple.developer.carplay-video</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
